{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790291254,"nonce":"K7gt571Jqr7sdR0uoDb5Qp8a/FU=","message":"The same entry path also skips the named fields: a computed string key that names a field of the constructor stores into that field untyped.\n\n    local k = (\"x\"):rep(1)\n    local u = {x = 1, [k] = 2.5}\n    print(u.x + 1)   -- lua5.4: 3.5; zylua: internal: a value of another kind stored into a shaped field\n\nReproduces on main 678f49eb. With the typed dynamic-key reads of package L-lattice-intornil-borrow, a string, boolean or table computed key in a constructor (`{[k] = 5}` then `t[k] or 0`) also reads as nil, because dyn_value never takes the entry.","files":null}]}